/-!
# Proposition C.4 (`ar:prop:convergence`): literal export

The target `plane_eisenstein_convergent_invariant` records the adelic summability and left-invariance of the Eisenstein
sum. This file states the proposition as it is written in the paper: the series

  `𝓔_P(ω_h) = ∑_{γ ∈ Γ_P\Γ} ρ(γ)⁻¹ γ^* ω_h`      (`ar:eq:Eseries`)

of the seed `ω_h = h(τ) 𝓑ⁿ (du₁ - τ du₂) ∧ dτ` of a cusp form `h = f ∘ ofComplex` converges
normally, with every derivative, on compact subsets of `𝒳`, and defines a smooth closed global
two-form with values in `E_n`, which is `Γ`-equivariant.

## Model
`𝒳 = SL₃(ℝ)/SO(3)` is identified with the open set `Ω = {p ∈ ℝ⁵ : p₃ > 0, p₄ > 0}` of plane
coordinates `(u₁, u₂, x, y, t)` through the Gram matrix `G = p pᵀ` (`planeGram`, `planePoint`): the
chart is a bijection from `Ω` to the positive definite determinant-one matrices
(`chart_left_inv`, `chart_right_inv`), and `SL₃(ℝ)` acts by `G ↦ g G gᵀ` (`planeAct`). A two-form on
`Ω` with values in `ℂ[X, Y, Z]` is a function `ω : ℝ⁵ → Fin 5 → Fin 5 → MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ`
(components `ω(∂ᵢ, ∂ⱼ)`), its pullback is `formPullback`, and the coefficient action is
`SeedC3.rho`. The summand attached to `γ ∈ Γ` is `summandPoly n h (realMat γ)`.

## Statements
* `normal_convergence`: for every compact `K ⊂ Ω` and every order `k`, one summable function on
  `Γ_P\Γ` bounds, uniformly on `K`, the `k`-th derivative of every coefficient of every
  component of every term.
* `planeEisenstein_smooth`, `planeEisenstein_derivative`: the sum is `C^∞` and its derivatives are the
  sums of the derivatives of the terms.
* `planeEisenstein_closed`: the coordinate form of `dE = 0`, with the same coordinate partial
  derivatives as the closedness clause of `seed_closed_equivariant`.
* `planeEisenstein_equivariant`, `planeEisenstein_pullback`: `ρ(δ)⁻¹ δ^* E = E`, i.e.
  `δ^* E = ρ(δ) E`, for `δ ∈ Γ`.
* `summand_stab_mul`, `planeEisenstein_section`: the term depends only on the coset `Γ_P γ`, and the
  sum may be computed with any set of representatives.
* `planeEisenstein_antisymm`, `planeEisenstein_diag`, `planeEisensteinForm`, `planeEisensteinForm_isAlt`,
  `planeEisensteinForm_smooth`: the components are antisymmetric in `(i, j)` and vanish for `i = j`,
  so they are the matrix of an alternating bilinear form on the tangent space `ℝ⁵` with values in
  `E_n` (`LinearMap.IsAlt`), smooth in the point (every coefficient, equivalently the coordinates in
  `ℂ^{monSet n} ≅ E_n`, `coords_injective`). The same for both seeds and every cusp
  (`planeEisensteinAt_antisymm`, `planeEisensteinAtForm_isAlt`, `planeEisensteinAtForm_smooth`).
* `prop_C_4_gammaN`: all of the above for the paper's `Γ = Γ(N)`, `3 ∣ N`
  (neat, normal in `K` and `K†`), where the compatibility `Λ_P = Γ₂(N)` of the cusp group with the
  Levi projection of `Γ_P` is a theorem, not a hypothesis. The hypothesis `LeviIn Γ Λ` of the
  parametric statements is exactly that compatibility.

## Antiholomorphic seeds and the other plane cusps
`prop_C_4_cusp_gammaN` (the statement is `PropC4Cusp`) gives the seven clauses for both types of
seed (`b = false`: holomorphic `ω_h`; `b = true`: antiholomorphic `ω̄_h`, the complex conjugate of the
coefficient polynomial and of the differential) at every plane cusp `h⁻¹ P h` of `Γ(N)`, `h ∈ SL₃(ℤ)`.
The series is `∑_{γ ∈ Γ_{P'}\Γ} ρ(hγ)⁻¹ (hγ)^* ω`, `Γ_{P'} = Γ ∩ h⁻¹ P(ℚ) h`, with the Levi data
`Λ_{P'} = Γ₂(N)` proved, not assumed. `prop_C_4_rational_cusp_gammaN` transports this to every
rational conjugate `g P g⁻¹`, `g ∈ GL₃(ℚ)`: such a cusp is `h⁻¹ P h` for an integral `h` (with
`Γ ∩ g P(ℚ) g⁻¹` equal to the cusp stabilizer). The parametric `*_at` statements hold for every cusp
datum `D` (`CuspData`: a real change of basis whose third row is a multiple of an integral row;
`CuspData.ofRational g` is the datum of `g ∈ GL₃(ℚ)` itself) under the hypothesis `LeviInCusp` on
the cusp group.

## The group
`gammaN_paper`: `Γ(N)`, `3 ∣ N`, is neat in the paper's sense (`IsNeat`: for each element
the subgroup of `ℂˣ` generated by its eigenvalues contains no nontrivial root of unity), normal in
`SL₃(ℤ)` and in `GL₃(ℤ)` (hence in `K` and `K†`), and contained in `K`.

Formalized by Claude Sonnet 5.5.
-/

open MvPolynomial UpperHalfPlane ModularForm
open scoped UpperHalfPlane MatrixGroups ContDiff

namespace TernaryPeriodPolynomials.Argument.Statements.ConvergenceC4

open TernaryPeriodPolynomials.Argument TernaryPeriodPolynomials.Argument.ConvergenceC4

noncomputable section

/-! ### The model: the global chart -/

/-- The chart `Ω → {Gram matrices}` is injective: `planePoint` is a left inverse. -/
theorem chart_left_inv {p : Fin 5 → ℝ} (hp : p ∈ Omega) : planePoint (planeGram p) = p :=
  planePoint_planeGram hp

/-- The chart is surjective onto the positive definite determinant-one matrices. -/
theorem chart_right_inv {G : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ} (hG : IsGram G) :
    planeGram (planePoint G) = G :=
  planeGram_planePoint hG

/-- The Gram matrices of points of `Ω` are positive definite of determinant one. -/
theorem chart_isGram {p : Fin 5 → ℝ} (hp : p ∈ Omega) : IsGram (planeGram p) :=
  planeGram_isGram hp

/-- `SL₃(ℝ)` acts on `Ω`. -/
theorem planeAct_mem_Omega {g : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℝ} (hg : g.det = 1) {p : Fin 5 → ℝ}
    (hp : p ∈ Omega) : planeAct g p ∈ Omega :=
  planeAct_mem hg hp

/-! ### The paper's group `Γ(N)` is neat, normal in `K` and `K†`, contained in `K` -/

/-- **`Γ(N)`, `3 ∣ N`, is a neat normal subgroup in the paper's sense.** For each element the
subgroup of `ℂˣ` generated by its eigenvalues has no nontrivial root of unity (`IsNeat`); the
subgroup is normal in `SL₃(ℤ)`, and hence in `K`, `K† = B₃ K B₃⁻¹` and every subgroup of `GL₃(ℤ)`
(`principal N` is normal in `GL₃(ℤ)`); and it lies in `K` for `3 ∣ N`. -/
theorem gammaN_paper (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (h3 : 3 ∣ N) :
    IsNeat (gammaN N) ∧ (gammaN N).Normal ∧
    (∀ g p : GL (Fin 3) ℤ, p ∈ TernaryPoly.IntegralGL3Congruence.principal N →
      g * p * g⁻¹ ∈ TernaryPoly.IntegralGL3Congruence.principal N) ∧
    (∀ γ ∈ gammaN N, Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.toGL γ ∈ TernaryPoly.ModThreeGoodAction.K) := by
  have hN : 3 ≤ N := Nat.le_of_dvd (Nat.pos_of_ne_zero (NeZero.ne N)) h3
  refine ⟨gammaN_isNeat hN, inferInstance, fun g p hp => ?_, fun γ hγ =>
    toGL_mem_K_of_mem_gammaN h3 hγ⟩
  exact (TernaryPoly.IntegralGL3Congruence.principal_normal N).conj_mem p hp g

/-! ### The global form -/

/-- The coefficient space `E_n`: homogeneous polynomials of degree `n` in three variables. -/
abbrev En (n : ℕ) : Submodule ℂ (MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ) :=
  MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin 3) ℂ n

/-- The coordinates of an element of `E_n` in the monomial basis (degree-`n` monomials). -/
def coords (n : ℕ) (P : En n) : monSet n → ℂ := fun m => (P : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m

/-- The coordinates determine the element of `E_n`: `E_n ≅ ℂ^{monSet n}` as vector spaces, so
smoothness of an `E_n`-valued map is smoothness of its coordinates. -/
theorem coords_injective (n : ℕ) : Function.Injective (coords n) := by
  intro P Q h
  apply Subtype.ext
  refine MvPolynomial.ext _ _ fun m => ?_
  by_cases hm : m ∈ monSet n
  · exact congrFun h ⟨m, hm⟩
  · have hP : (P : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m = 0 := by
      by_contra hne; exact hm (mem_monSet_of_coeff_ne P.2 hne)
    have hQ : (Q : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m = 0 := by
      by_contra hne; exact hm (mem_monSet_of_coeff_ne Q.2 hne)
    rw [hP, hQ]

section Parametric

variable (Γ : Subgroup (Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 3) ℤ))
  {F : Type*} [FunLike F ℍ ℂ] (Λ : Subgroup (GL (Fin 2) ℝ)) [Λ.HasDetOne] [Λ.IsArithmetic]
  (n : ℕ) [CuspFormClass F Λ ((n + 3 : ℕ) : ℤ)] (f : F)

/-- **The plane Eisenstein form `𝓔_P(ω_h)`** (`ar:eq:Eseries`) of the seed of the cusp form `f`, as an
`E_n`-valued function on `Ω` with components `E(∂ₐ, ∂_b)`: its coefficients are the sums
`∑_{γ ∈ Γ_P\Γ}` of the coefficients of the summands `ρ(γ)⁻¹ γ^* ω_h` (`summandPoly`). -/
def planeEisenstein (y : Fin 5 → ℝ) (a b : Fin 5) : En n :=
  ⟨seriesForm Γ n f y a b, seriesForm_isHomogeneous Γ n f y a b⟩

/-- The coefficients of `𝓔_P(ω_h)` are the sums over `Γ_P\Γ` of the coefficients of the terms. -/
theorem coeff_planeEisenstein (y : Fin 5 → ℝ) (a b : Fin 5) (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ) :
    ((planeEisenstein Γ n f y a b : En n) : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m =
      ∑' c : PlaneCoset Γ, termFun Γ n f c a b m y :=
  coeff_seriesForm Γ n f m y a b

/-- The term attached to a coset `Γ_P γ` is the summand `ρ(γ)⁻¹ γ^* ω_h` of a representative. -/
theorem termFun_def (c : PlaneCoset Γ) (a b : Fin 5) (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ) (y : Fin 5 → ℝ) :
    termFun Γ n f c a b m y =
      (SeedC3.rho (realMat (Quotient.out c).1)⁻¹
        (formPullback (planeAct (realMat (Quotient.out c).1))
          (seedForm n (fun z => f (ofComplex z))) y a b)).coeff m :=
  rfl

/-- **The sum is an alternating two-form: antisymmetry of the components.** -/
theorem planeEisenstein_antisymm (y : Fin 5 → ℝ) (a c : Fin 5) :
    planeEisenstein Γ n f y a c = - planeEisenstein Γ n f y c a :=
  Subtype.ext (seriesForm_antisymm Γ n f y a c)

theorem planeEisenstein_diag (y : Fin 5 → ℝ) (a : Fin 5) : planeEisenstein Γ n f y a a = 0 :=
  Subtype.ext (seriesForm_diag Γ n f y a)

/-- The alternating bilinear form `E_y(v, w) = ∑ v_a w_c E_{ac}(y)` on the tangent space `ℝ⁵`
with values in `E_n`, whose matrix in the coordinate basis is the component model. -/
def planeEisensteinForm (y : Fin 5 → ℝ) : (Fin 5 → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (Fin 5 → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] En n :=
  componentBil (planeEisenstein Γ n f y)

theorem planeEisensteinForm_single (y : Fin 5 → ℝ) (a c : Fin 5) :
    planeEisensteinForm Γ n f y (Pi.single a 1) (Pi.single c 1) = planeEisenstein Γ n f y a c :=
  componentBil_single _ a c

/-- **`E_y` is an alternating map on the tangent space.** -/
theorem planeEisensteinForm_isAlt (y : Fin 5 → ℝ) : LinearMap.IsAlt (planeEisensteinForm Γ n f y) :=
  componentBil_isAlt _ fun a c => by
    have := planeEisenstein_antisymm Γ n f y a c
    exact this

include Λ

omit [Λ.HasDetOne] in
/-- **Proposition C.4, normal convergence with every derivative.** For `n ≥ 4`, every compact
`K ⊂ Ω` and every order `k`, there is one summable function `b` on `Γ_P\Γ` with
`‖D^k (coefficient of the (i,j) component of the term of c)(x)‖ ≤ b c` for all `x ∈ K`, all
components and all coefficients. -/
theorem normal_convergence (hn : 4 ≤ n) {K : Set (Fin 5 → ℝ)} (hK : IsCompact K)
    (hKΩ : K ⊆ Omega) (k : ℕ) :
    ∃ b : PlaneCoset Γ → ℝ, Summable b ∧ ∀ (c : PlaneCoset Γ), ∀ x ∈ K, ∀ (i j : Fin 5)
      (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ), ‖iteratedFDeriv ℝ k (termFun Γ n f c i j m) x‖ ≤ b c :=
  exists_summable_jet_bound_all Γ Λ n f hn hK hKΩ k

omit [Λ.HasDetOne] in
/-- **Proposition C.4, smoothness.** Every coefficient of every component of `𝓔_P(ω_h)` is `C^∞` on
the open set `Ω`. -/
theorem planeEisenstein_smooth (hn : 4 ≤ n) (i j : Fin 5) (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ) :
    ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ (fun y => ((planeEisenstein Γ n f y i j : En n) :
      MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) Omega :=
  contDiffOn_seriesForm_coeff Γ Λ n f hn i j m

omit [Λ.HasDetOne] in
/-- **Proposition C.4, termwise differentiation.** Every derivative of the sum is the sum of the
derivatives of the terms. -/
theorem planeEisenstein_derivative (hn : 4 ≤ n) (k : ℕ) {x : Fin 5 → ℝ} (hx : x ∈ Omega)
    (i j : Fin 5) (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ) :
    iteratedFDeriv ℝ k (fun y => ((planeEisenstein Γ n f y i j : En n) :
        MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) x =
      ∑' c : PlaneCoset Γ, iteratedFDeriv ℝ k (termFun Γ n f c i j m) x := by
  have h := (seriesCoeff_smooth Γ Λ n f hn i j m).2 k x hx
  have e : (fun y => ((planeEisenstein Γ n f y i j : En n) :
      MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) = seriesCoeff Γ n f i j m :=
    funext fun y => coeff_seriesForm Γ n f m y i j
  rw [e]
  exact h

omit [Λ.HasDetOne] in
/-- **Proposition C.4, closedness.** `dE = 0`: for every point of `Ω`, every coefficient and all
`i, j, k`, `∂ᵢE_{jk} - ∂ⱼE_{ik} + ∂ₖE_{ij} = 0` (the same coordinate partial derivatives as in the
closedness clause of `seed_closed_equivariant`). -/
theorem planeEisenstein_closed (hn : 4 ≤ n) {x : Fin 5 → ℝ} (hx : x ∈ Omega) (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ)
    (i j k : Fin 5) :
    coordPartial (fun q => ((planeEisenstein Γ n f q j k : En n) :
        MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) i x -
      coordPartial (fun q => ((planeEisenstein Γ n f q i k : En n) :
        MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) j x +
      coordPartial (fun q => ((planeEisenstein Γ n f q i j : En n) :
        MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) k x = 0 :=
  seriesForm_closed Γ Λ n f hn hx m i j k

omit [Λ.IsArithmetic] in
/-- **Equivariance removes the choice of representative.** If the Levi blocks of the elements of
`Γ_P` lie in `Λ`, the term of a coset does not depend on the representative: for `γ` in the plane
stabilizer the summand at `γ δ` equals the summand at `δ`. -/
theorem summand_stab_mul
    (γ δ : Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 3) ℤ) (hγ : γ ∈ planeStab)
    (hΛ : ∃ g ∈ Λ, (g : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) = topBlock (realMat γ))
    {q : Fin 5 → ℝ} (hq : q ∈ Omega) (i j : Fin 5) :
    summandPoly n (fun z => f (ofComplex z)) (realMat (γ * δ)) q i j =
      summandPoly n (fun z => f (ofComplex z)) (realMat δ) q i j :=
  summandPoly_stab_mul Λ n f γ δ hγ hΛ hq i j

omit [Λ.IsArithmetic] in
/-- **The sum over `Γ_P\Γ` may be computed with any representatives.** -/
theorem planeEisenstein_section (hLevi : LeviIn Γ Λ) {x : Fin 5 → ℝ} (hx : x ∈ Omega)
    (i j : Fin 5) (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ) (r : PlaneCoset Γ → Γ)
    (hr : ∀ c, (Quotient.mk _ (r c) : PlaneCoset Γ) = c) :
    ((planeEisenstein Γ n f x i j : En n) : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m =
      ∑' c : PlaneCoset Γ,
        (SeedC3.rho (realMat (r c).1)⁻¹
          (formPullback (planeAct (realMat (r c).1)) (seedForm n (fun z => f (ofComplex z)))
            x i j)).coeff m := by
  rw [coeff_planeEisenstein]
  exact seriesCoeff_eq_tsum_section Γ Λ n f hLevi hx i j m r hr

/-- **Proposition C.4, `Γ`-equivariance of the global form.** For `δ ∈ Γ` and `x ∈ Ω`,
`ρ(δ)⁻¹ δ^* 𝓔_P(ω_h) = 𝓔_P(ω_h)`. -/
theorem planeEisenstein_equivariant (hn : 4 ≤ n) (hLevi : LeviIn Γ Λ) (δ : Γ) {x : Fin 5 → ℝ}
    (hx : x ∈ Omega) (i j : Fin 5) :
    SeedC3.rho (realMat δ.1)⁻¹ (formPullback (planeAct (realMat δ.1))
      (fun y a b => (planeEisenstein Γ n f y a b : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ)) x i j) =
      (planeEisenstein Γ n f x i j : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ) :=
  seriesForm_equivariant Γ Λ n f hn hLevi δ hx i j

/-- **Proposition C.4, `Γ`-equivariance, as a transformation law:** `δ^* 𝓔_P(ω_h) = ρ(δ) 𝓔_P(ω_h)`. -/
theorem planeEisenstein_pullback (hn : 4 ≤ n) (hLevi : LeviIn Γ Λ) (δ : Γ) {x : Fin 5 → ℝ}
    (hx : x ∈ Omega) (i j : Fin 5) :
    formPullback (planeAct (realMat δ.1))
      (fun y a b => (planeEisenstein Γ n f y a b : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ)) x i j =
      SeedC3.rho (realMat δ.1) (planeEisenstein Γ n f x i j : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ) :=
  seriesForm_pullback Γ Λ n f hn hLevi δ hx i j

omit [Λ.HasDetOne] in
/-- **The two-form is smooth in the point**: for all tangent vectors `v, w` every coefficient of
`E_y(v, w)` is `C^∞` on `Ω`. -/
theorem planeEisensteinForm_smooth (hn : 4 ≤ n) (v w : Fin 5 → ℝ) (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ) :
    ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ (fun y => ((planeEisensteinForm Γ n f y v w : En n) :
      MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) Omega :=
  contDiffOn_componentBil_coeff n Omega (planeEisenstein Γ n f)
    (fun a c m => planeEisenstein_smooth Γ Λ n f hn a c m) v w m

omit [Λ.HasDetOne] in
/-- The same, as a map into the finite-dimensional space `ℂ^{monSet n} ≅ E_n`. -/
theorem planeEisensteinForm_smooth_coords (hn : 4 ≤ n) (v w : Fin 5 → ℝ) :
    ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ (fun y => coords n (planeEisensteinForm Γ n f y v w)) Omega :=
  contDiffOn_pi.2 fun m => planeEisensteinForm_smooth Γ Λ n f hn v w m

end Parametric

/-! ### The paper's group `Γ = Γ(N)` -/

/-- **Proposition C.4 for the paper's group.** Let `Γ = Γ(N) ⊂ SL₃(ℤ)` be the principal
congruence subgroup of level `N`, `3 ∣ N` (neat, normal in `K` and `K†`), `Λ_P = Γ₂(N)` the Levi
projection of `Γ_P = Γ ∩ P(ℚ)`, `n ≥ 4`, and `f` a cusp form of weight `k = n + 3` for `Λ_P`. Then:

1. `Γ ∩ P(ℚ)` is the integral plane stabilizer, and `Λ_P = Γ₂(N)` is exactly its Levi projection;
2. the term of a coset does not depend on the representative;
3. the series converges normally with every derivative on every compact subset of `Ω ≅ 𝒳`;
4. its sum is a smooth `E_n`-valued two-form on `Ω`, differentiable termwise;
5. it is closed;
6. it is `Γ`-equivariant: `δ^* 𝓔 = ρ(δ) 𝓔` for every `δ ∈ Γ`.

Moreover `Γ(N)` is normal in `SL₃(ℤ)`, contained in `K`, and torsion-free
(`gammaN_normal`, `toGL_mem_K_of_mem_gammaN`, `gammaN_torsionFree`). -/
theorem prop_C_4_gammaN (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (h3 : 3 ∣ N) (n : ℕ) (hn : 4 ≤ n)
    (f : CuspForm (leviGroup N) ((n + 3 : ℕ) : ℤ)) :
    -- (1) the stabilizer of the rational plane, and the Levi projection
    (∀ γ ∈ gammaN N, γ ∈ planeStab ↔
      (γ : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℤ) 2 0 = 0 ∧ (γ : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℤ) 2 1 = 0) ∧
    (∀ g : GL (Fin 2) ℝ, g ∈ leviGroup N ↔ ∃ γ ∈ gammaN N, γ ∈ planeStab ∧
      (g : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) = topBlock (realMat γ)) ∧
    -- (2) independence of the coset representative
    (∀ γ ∈ gammaN N, γ ∈ planeStab → ∀ (δ : Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 3) ℤ) (q : Fin 5 → ℝ),
      q ∈ Omega → ∀ i j,
      summandPoly n (fun z => f (ofComplex z)) (realMat (γ * δ)) q i j =
        summandPoly n (fun z => f (ofComplex z)) (realMat δ) q i j) ∧
    -- (3) normal convergence of every derivative on compact sets
    (∀ K : Set (Fin 5 → ℝ), IsCompact K → K ⊆ Omega → ∀ k : ℕ,
      ∃ b : PlaneCoset (gammaN N) → ℝ, Summable b ∧ ∀ c, ∀ x ∈ K, ∀ (i j : Fin 5)
        (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ), ‖iteratedFDeriv ℝ k (termFun (gammaN N) n f c i j m) x‖ ≤ b c) ∧
    -- (4) smooth, differentiable termwise
    (∀ (i j : Fin 5) (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ), ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ (fun y => ((planeEisenstein (gammaN N) n f y i j :
      En n) : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) Omega) ∧
    (∀ (k : ℕ) (x : Fin 5 → ℝ), x ∈ Omega → ∀ (i j : Fin 5) (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ),
      iteratedFDeriv ℝ k (fun y => ((planeEisenstein (gammaN N) n f y i j : En n) :
        MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) x =
      ∑' c : PlaneCoset (gammaN N), iteratedFDeriv ℝ k (termFun (gammaN N) n f c i j m) x) ∧
    -- (5) closed
    (∀ x : Fin 5 → ℝ, x ∈ Omega → ∀ (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ) (i j k : Fin 5),
      coordPartial (fun q => ((planeEisenstein (gammaN N) n f q j k : En n) :
          MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) i x -
        coordPartial (fun q => ((planeEisenstein (gammaN N) n f q i k : En n) :
          MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) j x +
        coordPartial (fun q => ((planeEisenstein (gammaN N) n f q i j : En n) :
          MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) k x = 0) ∧
    -- (6) Γ-equivariant
    (∀ δ : gammaN N, ∀ x : Fin 5 → ℝ, x ∈ Omega → ∀ i j : Fin 5,
      formPullback (planeAct (realMat δ.1))
        (fun y a b => (planeEisenstein (gammaN N) n f y a b : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ)) x i j =
        SeedC3.rho (realMat δ.1) (planeEisenstein (gammaN N) n f x i j :
          MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ)) := by
  have hN : 3 ≤ N := Nat.le_of_dvd (Nat.pos_of_ne_zero (NeZero.ne N)) h3
  refine ⟨fun γ hγ => gammaN_inf_rationalPlane hN hγ, mem_leviGroup_iff N, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro γ hγ hs δ q hq i j
    exact summand_stab_mul (leviGroup N) n f γ δ hs (leviIn_gammaN N γ hγ hs) hq i j
  · intro K hK hKΩ k
    exact normal_convergence (gammaN N) (leviGroup N) n f hn hK hKΩ k
  · intro i j m
    exact planeEisenstein_smooth (gammaN N) (leviGroup N) n f hn i j m
  · intro k x hx i j m
    exact planeEisenstein_derivative (gammaN N) (leviGroup N) n f hn k hx i j m
  · intro x hx m i j k
    exact planeEisenstein_closed (gammaN N) (leviGroup N) n f hn hx m i j k
  · intro δ x hx i j
    exact planeEisenstein_pullback (gammaN N) (leviGroup N) n f hn (leviIn_gammaN N) δ hx i j

/-! ### Both seeds, every plane cusp -/

section Cusps

variable (b : Bool) (D : CuspData) (Γ : Subgroup (Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 3) ℤ))
  {F : Type*} [FunLike F ℍ ℂ] (Λ : Subgroup (GL (Fin 2) ℝ)) [Λ.HasDetOne] [Λ.IsArithmetic]
  (n : ℕ) [CuspFormClass F Λ ((n + 3 : ℕ) : ℤ)] (f : F)

/-- **The plane Eisenstein form at the cusp `D` for the seed of type `b`**:
`∑_{γ ∈ Γ_{P'}\Γ} ρ(aγ)⁻¹ (aγ)^* ω^b` (`summandK`), an `E_n`-valued function on `Ω`. -/
def planeEisensteinAt (y : Fin 5 → ℝ) (a c : Fin 5) : En n :=
  ⟨seriesFormK b D Γ n f y a c, seriesFormK_isHomogeneous b D Γ n f y a c⟩

theorem coeff_planeEisensteinAt (y : Fin 5 → ℝ) (a c : Fin 5) (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ) :
    ((planeEisensteinAt b D Γ n f y a c : En n) : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m =
      ∑' w : CuspCoset Γ D.r, termFunK b D Γ n f w a c m y :=
  coeff_seriesFormK b D Γ n f m y a c

/-- The term attached to a coset is the summand `ρ(aγ)⁻¹ (aγ)^* ω^b` of a representative. -/
theorem termFunK_def (w : CuspCoset Γ D.r) (a c : Fin 5) (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ) (y : Fin 5 → ℝ) :
    termFunK b D Γ n f w a c m y =
      (SeedC3.rho (D.a * realMat (Quotient.out w).1)⁻¹
        (formPullback (planeAct (D.a * realMat (Quotient.out w).1))
          (seedFormK b n (fun z => f (ofComplex z))) y a c)).coeff m :=
  rfl

/-- **The sum is an alternating two-form: antisymmetry of the components** (every plane cusp, both
seeds). -/
theorem planeEisensteinAt_antisymm (y : Fin 5 → ℝ) (a c : Fin 5) :
    planeEisensteinAt b D Γ n f y a c = - planeEisensteinAt b D Γ n f y c a :=
  Subtype.ext (seriesFormK_antisymm b D Γ n f y a c)

theorem planeEisensteinAt_diag (y : Fin 5 → ℝ) (a : Fin 5) : planeEisensteinAt b D Γ n f y a a = 0 :=
  Subtype.ext (seriesFormK_diag b D Γ n f y a)

/-- The alternating bilinear form `E_y(v, w) = ∑ v_a w_c E_{ac}(y)` on the tangent space `ℝ⁵` with
values in `E_n`. -/
def planeEisensteinAtForm (y : Fin 5 → ℝ) : (Fin 5 → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] (Fin 5 → ℝ) →ₗ[ℝ] En n :=
  componentBil (planeEisensteinAt b D Γ n f y)

theorem planeEisensteinAtForm_single (y : Fin 5 → ℝ) (a c : Fin 5) :
    planeEisensteinAtForm b D Γ n f y (Pi.single a 1) (Pi.single c 1) =
      planeEisensteinAt b D Γ n f y a c :=
  componentBil_single _ a c

/-- **`E_y` is an alternating map on the tangent space.** -/
theorem planeEisensteinAtForm_isAlt (y : Fin 5 → ℝ) :
    LinearMap.IsAlt (planeEisensteinAtForm b D Γ n f y) :=
  componentBil_isAlt _ fun a c => planeEisensteinAt_antisymm b D Γ n f y a c

include Λ

omit [Λ.HasDetOne] in
/-- **Normal convergence with every derivative** at the cusp `D`, for the seed of type `b`. -/
theorem normal_convergence_at (hn : 4 ≤ n) {K : Set (Fin 5 → ℝ)} (hK : IsCompact K)
    (hKΩ : K ⊆ Omega) (k : ℕ) :
    ∃ B : CuspCoset Γ D.r → ℝ, Summable B ∧ ∀ (w : CuspCoset Γ D.r), ∀ x ∈ K, ∀ (i j : Fin 5)
      (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ), ‖iteratedFDeriv ℝ k (termFunK b D Γ n f w i j m) x‖ ≤ B w :=
  exists_summable_jet_bound_all_K b D Γ Λ n f hn hK hKΩ k

omit [Λ.HasDetOne] in
/-- **Smoothness** of the sum. -/
theorem planeEisensteinAt_smooth (hn : 4 ≤ n) (i j : Fin 5) (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ) :
    ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ (fun y => ((planeEisensteinAt b D Γ n f y i j : En n) :
      MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) Omega :=
  contDiffOn_seriesFormK_coeff b D Γ Λ n f hn i j m

omit [Λ.HasDetOne] in
/-- **Termwise differentiation** of every order. -/
theorem planeEisensteinAt_derivative (hn : 4 ≤ n) (k : ℕ) {x : Fin 5 → ℝ} (hx : x ∈ Omega)
    (i j : Fin 5) (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ) :
    iteratedFDeriv ℝ k (fun y => ((planeEisensteinAt b D Γ n f y i j : En n) :
        MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) x =
      ∑' w : CuspCoset Γ D.r, iteratedFDeriv ℝ k (termFunK b D Γ n f w i j m) x := by
  have h := (seriesCoeffK_smooth b D Γ Λ n f hn i j m).2 k x hx
  have e : (fun y => ((planeEisensteinAt b D Γ n f y i j : En n) :
      MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) = seriesCoeffK b D Γ n f i j m :=
    funext fun y => coeff_seriesFormK b D Γ n f m y i j
  rw [e]
  exact h

omit [Λ.HasDetOne] in
/-- **Closedness** `dE = 0`, in the coordinate form of the `seed_closed_equivariant`. -/
theorem planeEisensteinAt_closed (hn : 4 ≤ n) {x : Fin 5 → ℝ} (hx : x ∈ Omega)
    (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ) (i j k : Fin 5) :
    coordPartial (fun q => ((planeEisensteinAt b D Γ n f q j k : En n) :
        MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) i x -
      coordPartial (fun q => ((planeEisensteinAt b D Γ n f q i k : En n) :
        MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) j x +
      coordPartial (fun q => ((planeEisensteinAt b D Γ n f q i j : En n) :
        MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) k x = 0 :=
  seriesFormK_closed b D Γ Λ n f hn hx m i j k

omit [Λ.IsArithmetic] in
/-- **Independence of the representatives.** -/
theorem planeEisensteinAt_section (hLevi : LeviInCusp D Γ Λ) {x : Fin 5 → ℝ} (hx : x ∈ Omega)
    (i j : Fin 5) (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ) (r : CuspCoset Γ D.r → Γ)
    (hr : ∀ w, (Quotient.mk _ (r w) : CuspCoset Γ D.r) = w) :
    ((planeEisensteinAt b D Γ n f x i j : En n) : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m =
      ∑' w : CuspCoset Γ D.r,
        (SeedC3.rho (D.a * realMat (r w).1)⁻¹
          (formPullback (planeAct (D.a * realMat (r w).1))
            (seedFormK b n (fun z => f (ofComplex z))) x i j)).coeff m := by
  rw [coeff_planeEisensteinAt]
  exact seriesCoeffK_eq_tsum_section b D Γ Λ n f hLevi hx i j m r hr

/-- **`Γ`-equivariance**: `ρ(δ)⁻¹ δ^* 𝓔 = 𝓔`. -/
theorem planeEisensteinAt_equivariant (hn : 4 ≤ n) (hLevi : LeviInCusp D Γ Λ) (δ : Γ)
    {x : Fin 5 → ℝ} (hx : x ∈ Omega) (i j : Fin 5) :
    SeedC3.rho (realMat δ.1)⁻¹ (formPullback (planeAct (realMat δ.1))
      (fun y a c => (planeEisensteinAt b D Γ n f y a c : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ)) x i j) =
      (planeEisensteinAt b D Γ n f x i j : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ) :=
  seriesFormK_equivariant b D Γ Λ n f hn hLevi δ hx i j

/-- **`Γ`-equivariance as a transformation law**: `δ^* 𝓔 = ρ(δ) 𝓔`. -/
theorem planeEisensteinAt_pullback (hn : 4 ≤ n) (hLevi : LeviInCusp D Γ Λ) (δ : Γ)
    {x : Fin 5 → ℝ} (hx : x ∈ Omega) (i j : Fin 5) :
    formPullback (planeAct (realMat δ.1))
      (fun y a c => (planeEisensteinAt b D Γ n f y a c : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ)) x i j =
      SeedC3.rho (realMat δ.1) (planeEisensteinAt b D Γ n f x i j : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ) :=
  seriesFormK_pullback b D Γ Λ n f hn hLevi δ hx i j

omit [Λ.HasDetOne] in
/-- **The two-form is smooth in the point**: for all tangent vectors `v, w` every coefficient of
`E_y(v, w)` is `C^∞` on `Ω`. -/
theorem planeEisensteinAtForm_smooth (hn : 4 ≤ n) (v w : Fin 5 → ℝ) (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ) :
    ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ (fun y => ((planeEisensteinAtForm b D Γ n f y v w : En n) :
      MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) Omega :=
  contDiffOn_componentBil_coeff n Omega (planeEisensteinAt b D Γ n f)
    (fun a c m => planeEisensteinAt_smooth b D Γ Λ n f hn a c m) v w m

omit [Λ.HasDetOne] in
/-- The same, as a map into the finite-dimensional space `ℂ^{monSet n} ≅ E_n`. -/
theorem planeEisensteinAtForm_smooth_coords (hn : 4 ≤ n) (v w : Fin 5 → ℝ) :
    ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ (fun y => coords n (planeEisensteinAtForm b D Γ n f y v w)) Omega :=
  contDiffOn_pi.2 fun m => planeEisensteinAtForm_smooth b D Γ Λ n f hn v w m.1

end Cusps

/-- **The statement of Proposition C.4 at the plane cusp `h⁻¹ P h` of `Γ(N)`**, for the seed of type
`b` of a cusp form `f` of weight `n + 3` for `Λ_P = Γ₂(N)`:

1. the cusp stabilizer `Γ_{P'}` is `Γ ∩ h⁻¹ P(ℚ) h`;
2. `Λ_P = Γ₂(N)` is exactly the Levi projection of `Γ_{P'}` (conjugated back to `P`);
3. the term of a coset does not depend on the representative;
4. the series converges normally with every derivative on every compact subset of `Ω ≅ 𝒳`;
5. its sum is a smooth `E_n`-valued two-form, differentiable termwise;
6. it is closed;
7. it is `Γ`-equivariant: `δ^* 𝓔 = ρ(δ) 𝓔` for every `δ ∈ Γ`. -/
def PropC4Cusp (N : ℕ) (h : Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 3) ℤ) (b : Bool) (n : ℕ)
    (f : CuspForm (leviGroup N) ((n + 3 : ℕ) : ℤ)) : Prop :=
    -- (1) the stabilizer of the rational plane
    (∀ p ∈ gammaN N, p ∈ stabRow (CuspData.ofSL h).r ↔
      ((h * p * h⁻¹ : Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 3) ℤ) : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℤ) 2 0 = 0 ∧
        ((h * p * h⁻¹ : Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 3) ℤ) : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℤ) 2 1 = 0) ∧
    -- (2) the Levi projection
    (∀ g : GL (Fin 2) ℝ, g ∈ leviGroup N ↔ ∃ p ∈ gammaN N, p ∈ stabRow (CuspData.ofSL h).r ∧
      (g : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ) =
        topBlock ((CuspData.ofSL h).a * realMat p * (CuspData.ofSL h).a⁻¹)) ∧
    -- (3) independence of the coset representative
    (∀ p ∈ gammaN N, p ∈ stabRow (CuspData.ofSL h).r →
      ∀ (γ : Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 3) ℤ) (q : Fin 5 → ℝ), q ∈ Omega → ∀ i j,
        summandK b n (fun z => f (ofComplex z)) ((CuspData.ofSL h).a * realMat (p * γ)) q i j =
          summandK b n (fun z => f (ofComplex z)) ((CuspData.ofSL h).a * realMat γ) q i j) ∧
    -- (4) normal convergence of every derivative on compact sets
    (∀ K : Set (Fin 5 → ℝ), IsCompact K → K ⊆ Omega → ∀ k : ℕ,
      ∃ B : CuspCoset (gammaN N) (CuspData.ofSL h).r → ℝ, Summable B ∧ ∀ w, ∀ x ∈ K,
        ∀ (i j : Fin 5) (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ),
          ‖iteratedFDeriv ℝ k (termFunK b (CuspData.ofSL h) (gammaN N) n f w i j m) x‖ ≤ B w) ∧
    -- (5) smooth, differentiable termwise
    (∀ (i j : Fin 5) (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ), ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ (fun y => ((planeEisensteinAt b
      (CuspData.ofSL h) (gammaN N) n f y i j : En n) : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) Omega) ∧
    (∀ (k : ℕ) (x : Fin 5 → ℝ), x ∈ Omega → ∀ (i j : Fin 5) (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ),
      iteratedFDeriv ℝ k (fun y => ((planeEisensteinAt b (CuspData.ofSL h) (gammaN N) n f y i j :
        En n) : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) x =
      ∑' w : CuspCoset (gammaN N) (CuspData.ofSL h).r,
        iteratedFDeriv ℝ k (termFunK b (CuspData.ofSL h) (gammaN N) n f w i j m) x) ∧
    -- (6) closed
    (∀ x : Fin 5 → ℝ, x ∈ Omega → ∀ (m : Fin 3 →₀ ℕ) (i j k : Fin 5),
      coordPartial (fun q => ((planeEisensteinAt b (CuspData.ofSL h) (gammaN N) n f q j k : En n) :
          MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) i x -
        coordPartial (fun q => ((planeEisensteinAt b (CuspData.ofSL h) (gammaN N) n f q i k :
          En n) : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) j x +
        coordPartial (fun q => ((planeEisensteinAt b (CuspData.ofSL h) (gammaN N) n f q i j :
          En n) : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ).coeff m) k x = 0) ∧
    -- (7) Γ-equivariant
    (∀ δ : gammaN N, ∀ x : Fin 5 → ℝ, x ∈ Omega → ∀ i j : Fin 5,
      formPullback (planeAct (realMat δ.1))
        (fun y a c => (planeEisensteinAt b (CuspData.ofSL h) (gammaN N) n f y a c :
          MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ)) x i j =
        SeedC3.rho (realMat δ.1) (planeEisensteinAt b (CuspData.ofSL h) (gammaN N) n f x i j :
          MvPolynomial (Fin 3) ℂ))

/-- **Proposition C.4 at every plane cusp of `Γ(N)`, for both seeds.** Let `Γ = Γ(N) ⊂ SL₃(ℤ)`,
`3 ∣ N`, `h ∈ SL₃(ℤ)` an integral change of basis (the plane cusp is `h⁻¹ P h`), `b` the type of
the seed (`false`: holomorphic `ω_h`, `true`: antiholomorphic `ω̄_h`), `n ≥ 4` and `f` a cusp form of
weight `n + 3` for `Λ_P = Γ₂(N)`. Then `PropC4Cusp N h b n f` (the seven clauses listed there). -/
theorem prop_C_4_cusp_gammaN (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (h3 : 3 ∣ N) (h : Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 3) ℤ)
    (b : Bool) (n : ℕ) (hn : 4 ≤ n) (f : CuspForm (leviGroup N) ((n + 3 : ℕ) : ℤ)) :
    PropC4Cusp N h b n f := by
  unfold PropC4Cusp
  have hN : 3 ≤ N := Nat.le_of_dvd (Nat.pos_of_ne_zero (NeZero.ne N)) h3
  have hL := leviInCusp_gammaN N h
  refine ⟨fun p hp => mem_stabRow_ofSL_iff_rational hN h hp, mem_leviGroup_iff_cusp N h, ?_, ?_,
    ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro p hp hs γ q hq i j
    exact summandK_cusp_stab (leviGroup N) n f b (CuspData.ofSL h) hL hp hs γ hq i j
  · intro K hK hKΩ k
    exact normal_convergence_at b (CuspData.ofSL h) (gammaN N) (leviGroup N) n f hn hK hKΩ k
  · intro i j m
    exact planeEisensteinAt_smooth b (CuspData.ofSL h) (gammaN N) (leviGroup N) n f hn i j m
  · intro k x hx i j m
    exact planeEisensteinAt_derivative b (CuspData.ofSL h) (gammaN N) (leviGroup N) n f hn k hx
      i j m
  · intro x hx m i j k
    exact planeEisensteinAt_closed b (CuspData.ofSL h) (gammaN N) (leviGroup N) n f hn hx m i j k
  · intro δ x hx i j
    exact planeEisensteinAt_pullback b (CuspData.ofSL h) (gammaN N) (leviGroup N) n f hn hL δ hx
      i j

/-- **Proposition C.4 at every rational plane cusp `g P g⁻¹`, `g ∈ GL₃(ℚ)`, of `Γ(N)`.** Every
rational plane cusp is an integral one: there is `h ∈ SL₃(ℤ)` with `h g ∈ P(ℚ)`, so that
`g P g⁻¹ = h⁻¹ P h`, the stabilizer `Γ ∩ g P(ℚ) g⁻¹` of the cusp in `Γ(N)` is the cusp stabilizer
of `h⁻¹ P h` (`g⁻¹ p g ∈ P(ℚ) ↔ p ∈ Γ_{P'}`), and for this cusp the seven clauses of Proposition C.4
hold for both types of seed and every cusp form `f` for `Λ_P = Γ₂(N)`. -/
theorem prop_C_4_rational_cusp_gammaN (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (h3 : 3 ∣ N) (g : GL (Fin 3) ℚ) :
    ∃ h : Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 3) ℤ,
      InPQ (((h : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℤ).map (Int.castRingHom ℚ)) *
        ((g : GL (Fin 3) ℚ) : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℚ)) ∧
      (∀ p ∈ gammaN N,
        InPQ (((g⁻¹ : GL (Fin 3) ℚ) : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℚ) *
          ((p : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℤ).map (Int.castRingHom ℚ)) *
          ((g : GL (Fin 3) ℚ) : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℚ)) ↔
        p ∈ stabRow (CuspData.ofSL h).r) ∧
      ∀ (b : Bool) (n : ℕ), 4 ≤ n → ∀ f : CuspForm (leviGroup N) ((n + 3 : ℕ) : ℤ),
        PropC4Cusp N h b n f := by
  have hN : 3 ≤ N := Nat.le_of_dvd (Nat.pos_of_ne_zero (NeZero.ne N)) h3
  obtain ⟨h, hh, hiff⟩ := rational_cusp_stabilizer g
  refine ⟨h, hh, fun p hp => ?_, fun b n hn f => prop_C_4_cusp_gammaN N h3 h b n hn f⟩
  rw [hiff p, cast_conj, inPQ_cast_iff]
  exact (mem_stabRow_ofSL_iff_rational hN h hp).symm

end

end TernaryPeriodPolynomials.Argument.Statements.ConvergenceC4
